  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$A x^{2}+B y^{2}=1$ ...(1)\r\n$A x+B y \\frac{d y}{d x}=0$ ...(2)\r\n$A+B y \\frac{d^{2} y}{d x^{2}}+B\\left(\\frac{d y}{d x}\\right)^{2}=0$ ...(3)\r\n$x\\left\\{-B y \\frac{d^{2} y}{d x^{2}}-B\\left(\\frac{d y}{d x}\\right)^{2}\\right\\}+B y \\frac{d y}{d x}=0$\r\nDividing both sides by $-\\mathrm{B}$, we get $x y \\frac{d^{2} y}{d x^{2}}+x\\left(\\frac{d y}{d x}\\right)^{2}-y \\frac{d y}{d x}=0$\r\nWhich is a DE of order 2 and degree 1",
    "image": null
  },
